# env files. Create React App loads .env, .env.development, .env.production and
# .env.test as well as the .local variants, and only the .local ones were ignored. In a
# demo, any of them is where a reader puts an API URL or a key, so ignore the lot and
# re-include the committed example.
.env*
!.env.example

